<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Smendes</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 1077–1052 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century-bce">11th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Smendes was a ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-egypt">Lower Egypt</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tanis">Tanis</a> at the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-kingdom-of-egypt">New Kingdom</a>, who founded the Twenty-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/old-babylonian-empire">First Dynasty</a>. By around 1100 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-egypt">Upper Egypt</a> was governed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/high-priest-of-amun">High Priest of Amun</a> while Smendes controlled Lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>. This division marked the end of the New Kingdom.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/smendes.jpg" alt="Smendes" width="315" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Metropolitan Museum of Art, New York · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Canopic_Smendes_Met.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
